The project keyword is used to include a CI/CD configuration file from another GitLab project (repository).

Simple definition:
project is used to import a .gitlab-ci.yml file from another GitLab project so that the same pipeline configuration can be reused.


2. Component Definition (in include)

The component keyword is used to include a predefined reusable CI/CD component from a component repository.

Simple definition:
component is used to include a reusable CI/CD pipeline component that performs a specific task, like build, test, or deploy.
